   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( f(x) = \\frac{\\left(x^{2} - 9 x + 18\\right)\\left(x^{2} + 4 x + 3\\right)}{\\left(x^{2} - 3 x - 18\\right)\\left(x^{2} + x - 12\\right)} \\). The graph of \\( f \\) has exactly one vertical asymptote, the line \\( x = c \\). Find the value of \\( c \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator factors as \\( \\left(x - 6\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) \\left(x + 1\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) \\) and the denominator as \\( \\left(x - 6\\right) \\left(x - 3\\right) \\left(x + 3\\right) \\left(x + 4\\right) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               6
            ],
            [
               "Subtract",
               "x",
               3
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The factors at \\( x = -3 \\), \\( x = 3 \\), and \\( x = 6 \\) divide out, so \\( f(x) = \\frac{x + 1}{x + 4} \\) for \\( x \\neq -3, 3, 6 \\). Those three inputs are removable discontinuities, not asymptotes.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               1
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               4
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "After cancelling, the denominator is zero only at \\( x = -4 \\), and the numerator is not zero there.",
         "mathjson": -4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The one sided limits are \\( \\lim_{x \\to -4^-} f(x) = \\infty \\) and \\( \\lim_{x \\to -4^+} f(x) = -\\infty \\).",
         "mathjson": -4
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "So the line \\( x = -4 \\) is the only vertical asymptote, and \\( c = -4 \\).",
         "mathjson": -4
      }
   ],
